{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"7d36e70a128a2bf3452249646614db7f3cb9795768b8b71a0387835a72306661","packTokens":2691,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":299,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":728,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1510,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"failures","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build a web app for Hive Works with two screens: a filtered requests list and request detail.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Store requests with the specified fields and validation, persistence, and exactly 8 seeded requests.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide exactly four API operations: list, create, get by ID, and change status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Enforce request validation, initial Open status, allowed status transitions, and immutable fields with no deletion.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement the list screen, status filters, creation dialog, loading/empty/error states, and responsive request rows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement request detail, status actions, update failure behavior, and not-found behavior.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Apply the specified light visual design, accessible controls, badges, and responsive layouts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Add automated business-rule tests and the specified end-to-end workflow test.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How should leading/trailing whitespace be handled for title and description validation and storage?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Trim leading/trailing whitespace before validation and storage; treat a resulting blank title as missing.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which browsers must the web app support?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No additional browser commitment; target a modern browser.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If multiple requests have the same creation timestamp, how should their relative order be determined in the newest-first list?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Their relative order is unspecified and may vary.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"If creating a request fails for a reason other than field validation (for example, a network or server error), what should the dialog do?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Show a generic creation error, keep the dialog open with its values, and allow another submission.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"If loading a detail address fails for a reason other than an unknown ID, what should the detail screen show?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Show a generic loading error with a Retry action; reserve “Request not found.” for unknown IDs.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"When the app starts with an already-populated database, how should the eight seed requests be handled?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Insert the eight seed requests only when initializing an empty database; preserve all requests on restarts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"After successfully creating a request while a status filter other than All is selected, what should happen to the filter and list?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Switch the filter to All so the new Open request appears at the top.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"When the user follows the detail screen's Back link, should the list retain the previously selected status filter?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Retain the filter selected before opening the detail screen.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 25 requirements as one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the 25-requirement scope be handled for this run?\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the 1280 px wide-layout viewport be a fixed requirement or configurable?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep 1280 px as a fixed required viewport width.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build the Hive Works maintenance app with exactly two screens—Requests and Request detail—for demo user Sam Carter (SC), without sign-in or role-selection screens.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Define only maintenance request records with a system-generated ID, UTC creation timestamp, required title, area, priority, and status, and optional description.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Trim leading and trailing whitespace from title and description before validation and storage, and treat a title that is blank after trimming as missing.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Accept titles of 3–80 characters, areas Kitchen, Meeting room, Open desk, Washroom, and Reception, priorities Low, Normal, and Urgent, and optional descriptions up to 500 characters; return validation messages naming each invalid field.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"On creation, set status to Open and assign the ID and UTC creation timestamp in the API, regardless of caller-supplied values for those fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Initialize an empty database with exactly eight seed requests: four Open, including one Urgent, two In progress, and two Done, with every supported area represented; preserve all requests and add no seeds when the database is nonempty.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Expose exactly four API operations: list requests with an optional status filter, create a request, get a request by ID, and change a request’s status; prevent changes to title, area, priority, and description after creation, and expose no deletion operation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"List all requests or only those matching an optional single status, newest first by creation timestamp, without guaranteeing order among equal timestamps.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Return the matching record when a requested ID exists and report not found otherwise.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Allow only Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open status transitions; reject all other status-change requests, including unknown IDs and unsupported status values, without changing any existing stored status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Show the Hive Works wordmark, SC, mutually exclusive All, Open, In progress, and Done filters with All selected by default, and a New request button on the Requests screen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Show each matching request’s title, area, priority badge, status badge, and UTC creation date in date-only form, newest first, and open its detail screen when selected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Open a creation dialog from New request with labeled Title, Area, Priority, and Description fields, supported Area and Priority choices, Normal selected by default, and Create and Cancel buttons.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Keep the creation dialog open when field validation fails and show each validation message beneath its field.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"After successful creation, close the dialog and show the new Open request at the top of the list, selecting All if another filter was active.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Disable Create and prevent duplicate create calls while a create request is pending; after a non-validation failure, show a generic error, retain the dialog and entered values, and allow another submission.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Show “Loading requests…” while the list is loading, “No requests here.” when empty for the selected filter, and “Could not load requests.” with Retry on failure.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Show a Back link, request title, area, priority and status badges, UTC creation date in date-only form, and the description or “No description.” on the detail screen; Back returns to the list with its prior filter selected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Show Start work for Open requests, Mark done for In progress requests, and Reopen for Done requests; update the status badge and action button only after a successful status-change response.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"On status-update failure, show “Could not update the request.” and retain the previously displayed status and action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"For an unknown ID, show “Request not found.” with a link to Requests; for other detail-loading failures, show a generic loading error with Retry, not “Request not found.”.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Use one light theme with a neutral background, near-black text, one primary-button brand color, one sans-serif font, Open blue badges, In progress amber badges, Done green badges, Urgent red badges, and neutral Low and Normal badges; show text on every badge.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Provide labeled fields and keyboard-reachable controls on both screens; use stacked request cards at 375 px and a request table at 1280 px, without horizontal page scrolling.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Include automated tests for request creation and validation, all allowed and disallowed status transitions, filtered newest-first listing, and unknown-ID handling.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"Include an end-to-end test for creating a request, opening its detail, changing status through Start work and Mark done, and filtering by Done.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"Ensure text and control contrast meets WCAG AA thresholds on the light theme.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<failures>\nYour previous attempt was rejected for these reasons. Fix them:\n- [spec-lint L8 anchors] REQ-23 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code\n</failures>\n\nMap the sentences."}